language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ prod: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Consider a set of products j. Each product has a coefficient a[j], a profit c[j] per unit and an upper
$ bound u[j] on its quantity. A shared limit b applies to the sum of the quantities divided by their coefficients a[j].
$ Choose the quantity of each product, within its bound, so that the total profit is as large as possible.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `prod.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/prod.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `prod_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py prod.json
$   savilerow model.eprime prod_1.param -run-solver

$ a_dim1: the number of products (derived from the data)
given a_dim1 : int
$ a[j]: the (positive) coefficient of product j; product j uses 1/a[j] of the shared limit per unit (indices from 1)
given a : matrix indexed by [int(1..a_dim1)] of int(1..)
$ c[j]: the profit per unit of product j
given c : matrix indexed by [int(1..a_dim1)] of int
$ u[j]: the largest quantity of product j
given u : matrix indexed by [int(1..a_dim1)] of int(0..)
$ b: the shared limit on the sum of the quantities divided by their coefficients
given b : int

$ the largest possible total profit in absolute value: a bound for total_profit
letting max_profit = sum j : int(1..a_dim1) . |c[j]| * u[j]

$ x[j]: the quantity of product j to produce (indices from 1)
find x : matrix indexed by [int(1..a_dim1)] of int(0..max(u))
$ total_profit: the total profit of the quantities produced
find total_profit : int(-max_profit..max_profit)

maximising total_profit
such that
$ the quantity of each product is at most its bound
forAll j : int(1..a_dim1) . x[j] <= u[j],
$ the sum of x[j]/a[j] is at most b; multiplying through by product(a) makes every coefficient a whole number
(sum j : int(1..a_dim1) . x[j] * (product(a) / a[j])) <= b * product(a),
$ the total profit is the sum of c[j] times x[j]
total_profit = (sum j : int(1..a_dim1) . c[j] * x[j])
